(1104396, 131991, 29168, '<td valign="top">Wow. I''m in shock. 12th place! <br/> <br/>Thanks for all the wonderful comments. graphicfunk - I love your portfolio - I''m honoured to receive such a compliment from you. I think I spent more time capturing this shot than any other in the past. Seems it was worth it.<br/> <br/>The place is "Whangarei Falls". It''s a smallish water fall on the edge of a volcano lava flow (so my Geography teacher told me) in my home town where I grew up. <br/> <br/>The water falls into a sort of deepish round "hole" area (40m wide?) leading to some rather nice light/shading effects at times.<br/> <br/>It has always been a favourite location of mine. It somehow oozes peace and calmness.<br/> <br/>"Waldo" was a fluke. At the time I was frustrated he was in the shot at all and took several, timed to hide him behind the undergrowth as he moved around looking for his own cool photo. I just happened to take the photo within the submission dates for this challenge. I nearly deleted it before I noticed the new challenge title!<br/></td>', 'Wow. I''m in shock. 12th place!  Thanks for all the wonderful comments. graphicfunk - I love your portfolio - I''m honoured to receive such a compliment from you. I think I spent more time capturing this shot than any other in the past. Seems it was worth it. The place is "Whangarei Falls". It''s a smallish water fall on the edge of a volcano lava flow (so my Geography teacher told me) in my home town where I grew up.  The water falls into a sort of deepish round "hole" area (40m wide?) leading to some rather nice light/shading effects at times. It has always been a favourite location of mine. It somehow oozes peace and calmness. "Waldo" was a fluke. At the time I was frustrated he was in the shot at all and took several, timed to hide him behind the undergrowth as he moved around looking for his own cool photo. I just happened to take the photo within the submission dates for this challenge. I nearly deleted it before I noticed the new challenge title!', '2005-01-12 15:49:12.000000', NULL, 0),
